///
/// @param[in] fileData File contents as an in-memory byte array.
/// @param[in] bakeScale Scale to bake into the shape or (1, 1, 1) for no change. Negative scale results in mirroring.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" that can be used to create actors.
///
/// @note The shape remains in memory while referenced by any handle or actor. In the C API, you must release the shape explicitly by calling @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "Context::ReleaseShape". In C++ and Python, this is optional, since @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" cleanup is automatic.
/// @note Some shape data cannot bake arbitrary non-uniform scale. Unsupported scale values are rejected.
/// @note Precomputed grid SDF data is preserved only when @p bakeScale is uniform by absolute value. Non-uniform scale by absolute value discards the precomputed SDF. If an SDF collider later requires SDF data, SuperDex Physics regenerates it from the transformed mesh at runtime, which may be expensive.
/// @note If the loaded model has @ref mochi::ModelData::elementFrameAxes "ModelData::elementFrameAxes", @p bakeScale transforms those axes as normal directions using the inverse-transpose of the scale transform, then normalize them.
/// @note Call on any thread.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle", @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "ReleaseShape", @ref mochi::Context::LoadShapeFromFile "LoadShapeFromFile"
///

/// @fn ShapeHandle mochi::Context::LoadShapeFromBytes(Span<char const> fileData, TransformRT const& bakeTransform, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Load a shape from a file of supported format, where the file has already been loaded into memory, and baking in rotation and translation.
///
