/// @note Call on any thread.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle", @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "ReleaseShape", @ref mochi::Context::LoadShapeFromFile "LoadShapeFromFile"
///

/// @fn ShapeHandle mochi::Context::LoadShapeFromBytes(Span<char const> fileData, MeshFileType format, Real3 const& bakeScale, TransformRT const& bakeTransform, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Load a shape from a file of supported format, where the file has already been loaded into memory, with an explicit mesh format hint, and baking in some scale, rotation, and translation.
///
/// @param[in] fileData File contents as an in-memory byte array.
/// @param[in] format Mesh file format hint. When @ref mochi::MeshFileType::Legacy "MeshFileType::Legacy", auto-detects between HDF5 and JSON via header bytes. When a surface mesh format (@ref mochi::MeshFileType::PLY "MeshFileType::PLY", @ref mochi::MeshFileType::OFF "MeshFileType::OFF", @ref mochi::MeshFileType::STL "MeshFileType::STL", @ref mochi::MeshFileType::OBJ "MeshFileType::OBJ"), dispatches directly to that reader.
/// @param[in] bakeScale Scale to bake into the shape or (1, 1, 1) for no change. Negative scale results in mirroring.
/// @param[in] bakeTransform Transform to bake into the shape, or the identity transform for no change.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" that can be used to create actors.
///
/// @note The shape remains in memory while referenced by any handle or actor. In the C API, you must release the shape explicitly by calling @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "Context::ReleaseShape". In C++ and Python, this is optional, since @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" cleanup is automatic.
/// @note Some shape data cannot bake arbitrary non-uniform scale. Unsupported scale values are rejected.
/// @note Precomputed grid SDF data is preserved only when @p bakeScale is uniform by absolute value. Non-uniform scale by absolute value discards the precomputed SDF. If an SDF collider later requires SDF data, SuperDex Physics regenerates it from the transformed mesh at runtime, which may be expensive.
/// @note If the loaded model has @ref mochi::ModelData::elementFrameAxes "ModelData::elementFrameAxes", @p bakeScale and @p bakeTransform transform those axes as normal directions using the inverse-transpose of the scale-rotation transform, then normalize them.
/// @note Call on any thread.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle", @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "ReleaseShape", @ref mochi::Context::LoadShapeFromFile "LoadShapeFromFile"
///

/// @fn ShapeHandle mochi::Context::CreateMeshShape(MeshData const& mesh, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Create a shape using in-memory mesh data, so that it can be used to create actors.
///
/// @param[in] mesh The mesh data, which SuperDex Physics copies.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" that can be used to create actors.
///
/// @note The shape remains in memory while referenced by any handle or actor. In the C API, you must release the shape explicitly by calling @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "Context::ReleaseShape". In C++ and Python, this is optional, since @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" cleanup is automatic.
/// @note Call on any thread.
/// @note Can be a tetrahedral mesh, a triangular mesh, or a polyline mesh, depending on the value of @ref mochi::MeshData::nodesPerElement "MeshData::nodesPerElement".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle", @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "ReleaseShape"
///

/// @fn ShapeHandle mochi::Context::CreateMeshShape(MeshDataView const& mesh, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Create a shape using in-memory mesh data, so that it can be used to create actors.
///
/// @param[in] mesh A non-owning view of the mesh data, which SuperDex Physics copies.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" that can be used to create actors.
///
/// @note The shape remains in memory while referenced by any handle or actor. In the C API, you must release the shape explicitly by calling @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "Context::ReleaseShape". In C++ and Python, this is optional, since @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" cleanup is automatic.
/// @note Call on any thread.
/// @note Can be a tetrahedral mesh, a triangular mesh, or a polyline mesh, depending on the value of @ref mochi::MeshDataView::nodesPerElement "MeshDataView::nodesPerElement".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle", @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "ReleaseShape"
///

/// @fn ShapeHandle mochi::Context::CreateModelShape(ModelData const& model, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Create a shape using in-memory model data, so that it can be used to create actors.
///
/// @param[in] model The model data, which SuperDex Physics copies.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" that can be used to create actors.
///
/// @note The shape remains in memory while referenced by any handle or actor. In the C API, you must release the shape explicitly by calling @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "Context::ReleaseShape". In C++ and Python, this is optional, since @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" cleanup is automatic.
/// @note Call on any thread.
/// @note Can be a mesh or an implicit shape, depending on the contents.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle", @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "ReleaseShape"
///

/// @fn ShapeHandle mochi::Context::CreateModelShape(ModelDataView const& model, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Create a shape using in-memory model data, so that it can be used to create actors.
///
/// @param[in] model A non-owning view of the model data, which SuperDex Physics copies.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" that can be used to create actors.
///
/// @note The shape remains in memory while referenced by any handle or actor. In the C API, you must release the shape explicitly by calling @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "Context::ReleaseShape". In C++ and Python, this is optional, since @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" cleanup is automatic.
/// @note Call on any thread.
/// @note Can be a mesh or an implicit shape, depending on the contents.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle", @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "ReleaseShape"
///

/// @fn ShapeHandle mochi::Context::CreateTetMeshShape(Span<real const> coordinates, Span<int const> connectivity, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Create a tetrahedral mesh shape using in-memory data.
///
/// @param[in] coordinates Node positions [m] (3 values per node)
/// @param[in] connectivity Node indices (4 values per tetrahedron).
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" that can be used to create actors.
///
/// @note The shape remains in memory while referenced by any handle or actor. In the C API, you must release the shape explicitly by calling @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "Context::ReleaseShape". In C++ and Python, this is optional, since @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" cleanup is automatic.
/// @note Call on any thread.
/// @note "Vertex" is another word for "node" in this context.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle", @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "ReleaseShape"
///

/// @fn ShapeHandle mochi::Context::CreateTriMeshShape(Span<real const> coordinates, Span<int const> connectivity, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Create a triangle mesh shape using in-memory data.
///
/// @param[in] coordinates Node positions [m] (3 values per node).
/// @param[in] connectivity Node indices (3 values per triangle).
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" that can be used to create actors.
///
/// @note The shape remains in memory while referenced by any handle or actor. In the C API, you must release the shape explicitly by calling @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "Context::ReleaseShape". In C++ and Python, this is optional, since @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" cleanup is automatic.
/// @note Call on any thread.
/// @note "Vertex" is another word for "node" in this context.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle", @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "ReleaseShape"
///

/// @fn ShapeHandle mochi::Context::CreateSphereShape(Real3 const& center, real radius, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Create an implicit sphere shape.
///
/// @param[in] center Center of the sphere [m], in the shape's local frame.
/// @param[in] radius Radius of the sphere [m]
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" that can be used to create rigid actors.
///
/// @note The shape remains in memory while referenced by any handle or actor. In the C API, you must release the shape explicitly by calling @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "Context::ReleaseShape". In C++ and Python, this is optional, since @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" cleanup is automatic.
/// @note Call on any thread.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle", @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "ReleaseShape"
///

/// @fn ShapeHandle mochi::Context::CreatePlaneShape(Real3 const& normal, real distance, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Create an implicit plane with infinite extents.
///
/// @param[in] normal Normal vector of the plane, in the shape's local frame. Need not be unit length; it is normalized internally.
/// @param[in] distance Signed offset [m] from the origin to the plane, measured along the (normalized) @p normal. The plane equation is dot(normalize(normal), x) = distance.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" that can be used to create rigid actors.
///
/// @note The shape remains in memory while referenced by any handle or actor. In the C API, you must release the shape explicitly by calling @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "Context::ReleaseShape". In C++ and Python, this is optional, since @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" cleanup is automatic.
/// @note Call on any thread.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle", @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "ReleaseShape"
///

/// @fn MeshDataView mochi::Context::GetShapeMesh(ShapeHandle shape, Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get a view of the shape's main mesh data.
///
/// @details For tetrahedral mesh shapes, returns the volume mesh (4 nodes per element). For triangular mesh shapes, returns the surface mesh (3 nodes per element). For polyline shapes, returns the polyline mesh (2 nodes per element). For shapes without a main mesh, including implicit shapes such as spheres and planes, returns an empty view.
///
/// @param[in] shape Handle to a valid shape.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A non-owning view of the shape's main mesh data, or an empty view if the shape has no mesh.
///
/// @note Can be called on any thread.
/// @note The returned view will be invalid after the shape handle has been released.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::MeshDataView "MeshDataView", @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeSurfaceMesh "GetShapeSurfaceMesh", @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeVisualMesh "GetShapeVisualMesh", @ref mochi::Actor::GetMesh "Actor::GetMesh"
///

/// @fn MeshDataView mochi::Context::GetShapeSurfaceMesh(ShapeHandle shape, Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get a view of the shape's surface mesh data.
///
/// @details Returns a triangle mesh (3 nodes per element) representing the shape's surface. The coordinate array contains exactly the surface nodes referenced by the returned connectivity; nodes present in the underlying main mesh but not referenced by any surface triangle are omitted. Connectivity values are indices into this returned coordinate array. For shapes without a surface mesh, returns an empty view.
///
/// @param[in] shape Handle to a valid shape.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A non-owning view of the shape's surface mesh data, or an empty view if the shape has no surface mesh.
///
/// @note For triangular mesh shapes, this may differ from @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeMesh "GetShapeMesh" if the main mesh contains unreferenced nodes. For tetrahedral mesh shapes, this is the boundary surface of the volume mesh, with non-boundary volume nodes omitted.
/// @note Can be called on any thread.
/// @note The returned view will be invalid after the shape handle has been released.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::MeshDataView "MeshDataView", @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeMesh "GetShapeMesh", @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeVisualMesh "GetShapeVisualMesh", @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMesh "Actor::GetSurfaceMesh"
///

/// @fn MeshDataView mochi::Context::GetShapeVisualMesh(ShapeHandle shape, Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get a view of the shape's visual mesh data, including skinning data if available.
///
/// @details Returns a triangle mesh (3 nodes per element) intended for visual rendering. Coordinates and connectivity are returned in visual-mesh node-index space, including any visual mesh nodes not referenced by the visual connectivity. The mesh may include linear skinning data for deformation. For shapes without a visual mesh, returns an empty view.
///
/// @param[in] shape Handle to a valid shape.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A non-owning view of the shape's visual mesh data, or an empty view if the shape has no visual mesh.
///
/// @note Can be called on any thread.
/// @note The returned view will be invalid after the shape handle has been released.
/// @note When linear visual-mesh skinning data is present, skinning indices refer to the node ordering returned by @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeMesh "GetShapeMesh", not to the compact surface-node ordering returned by @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeSurfaceMesh "GetShapeSurfaceMesh". Rod visual mesh embeddings are nonlinear and are not exposed through this linear skinning field.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::MeshDataView "MeshDataView", @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeMesh "GetShapeMesh", @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeSurfaceMesh "GetShapeSurfaceMesh", @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMesh "Actor::GetVisualMesh"
///

/// @fn Aabb mochi::Context::GetShapeAabb(ShapeHandle shape, Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get an axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) that contains the shape, in its local coordinate frame.
///
/// @param[in] shape Handle to a valid shape.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return The axis-aligned bounding box of the shape in local coordinates.
///
/// @note Call on any thread.
/// @note Sets an error for shapes that do not have a bounding volume (e.g., articulated shapes — query their link shapes individually instead).
///

/// @fn ArticulatedShapeInfo mochi::Context::GetArticulatedShapeInfo(ShapeHandle shape, Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get information about an articulated shape.
///
/// @param[in] shape Handle to an articulated shape.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return The @ref mochi::ArticulatedShapeInfo "ArticulatedShapeInfo" for the specified shape.
///
/// @note Only supported for articulated shapes. Sets error otherwise.
/// @note Can be called on any thread.
/// @note The returned information will be invalid after the shape handle has been released.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ArticulatedShapeInfo "ArticulatedShapeInfo", @ref mochi::Actor::GetArticulatedShapeInfo "Actor::GetArticulatedShapeInfo"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Context::ReleaseShape(ShapeHandle shape)
///
/// @brief Release a shape handle.
///
/// @details In the C API, this must be called for every @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" when you are done with it. In C++ and Python, this is optional because @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" releases its reference automatically when destroyed. The shape memory is freed when it is no longer referenced by any handle, actor, or file cache entry.
///
/// @param[in] shape Handle to the shape to release.
///
/// @note Call on any thread.
/// @note If the shape handle is invalid or already released, then it will be ignored.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle", @ref mochi::Context::IsFileCacheEnabled "IsFileCacheEnabled"
///

/// @fn int mochi::Context::GetNumShapes() const
///
/// @brief Get the number of shape handles that have been created/loaded and have not yet been released.
///
/// @return The number of active shape handles.
///
/// @note The file cache does not affect this value.
/// @note Call on any thread.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Context::IsFileCacheEnabled "IsFileCacheEnabled"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Context::EnableFileCache(bool enable)
///
/// @brief Enable or disable the file cache.
///
/// @details When enabled, shape memory will be preserved even after the @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" has been released. Subsequent requests for the same file (with the same baked-in scale and transform) will be fast because the data will already be loaded. This can be an important optimization, but beware that it could waste memory if it preserves shapes that are no longer needed.
///
/// @param[in] enable True to enable, false to disable the feature.
///
/// @note Call on any thread.
/// @note Disabling the cache (passing false) immediately releases all currently cached shapes, equivalent to calling @ref mochi::Context::ClearFileCache "ClearFileCache".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Context::IsFileCacheEnabled "IsFileCacheEnabled", @ref mochi::Context::ClearFileCache "ClearFileCache", @ref mochi::Context::ClearFileFromCache "ClearFileFromCache"
///

/// @fn bool mochi::Context::IsFileCacheEnabled() const
///
/// @brief Return true if the file cache feature is enabled.
///
/// @return True if the file cache is enabled, false otherwise.
///
/// @note Call on any thread.
///

/// @fn void mochi::Context::ClearFileCache()
///
/// @brief Release all shapes that are being preserved by the file cache (if any).
///
/// @details Use this to free up memory, or to force subsequent file requests to be loaded from disk, in case those files had been modified.
///
/// @note Call on any thread.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Context::IsFileCacheEnabled "IsFileCacheEnabled", @ref mochi::Context::ClearFileFromCache "ClearFileFromCache"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Context::ClearFileFromCache(std::string_view filePath)
///
/// @brief Release all cached entries for a given shape file.
///
/// @details Use this to free up memory, or to force the next file request to be loaded from disk, in case the file had been modified. All entries for @p filePath are removed, including every variant produced by different bake scale/transform combinations.
///
/// @param[in] filePath Path to a file that may have been loaded. The match is case-sensitive and must equal the path used at load time exactly.
///
/// @note Call on any thread.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Context::IsFileCacheEnabled "IsFileCacheEnabled", @ref mochi::Context::ClearFileCache "ClearFileCache"
///

/// @fn Scene* mochi::Context::CreateScene(std::string_view name)
///
/// @brief Create a new @ref mochi::Scene "Scene".
///
/// @details A scene is a collection of actors and constraints, which can be stepped to advance the simulation. Each scene is independent. Actors from one scene cannot affect another scene.
///
/// You can create a new scene on any thread, but that scene must only be accessed from one thread at a time. All reads and writes to the scene must be synchronous and well ordered. However, if you have multiple scenes, then it is safe to step them concurrently.
///
/// @param[in] name Name of the new scene (for debugging).
/// @return Pointer to the new scene. Call @ref mochi::Context::DestroyScene "DestroyScene" when done with it.
///
/// @note Call on any thread.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Context::DestroyScene "DestroyScene"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Context::DestroyScene(Scene* scene)
///
/// @brief Immediately destroy a scene and all its actors and constraints.
///
/// @param[in] scene Pointer to the scene to destroy.
///
/// @note No-op if @p scene is null or unknown to this @ref mochi::Context "Context".
/// @note Call on any thread.
/// @note Any remaining scenes will be cleaned up automatically when the @ref mochi::Context "Context" is destroyed.
///
/// @warning Do not dereference pointers to the scene, actors, constraints, etc. after this call.
/// @warning If @p scene is owned by an @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene", the call is a no-op (a warning is logged). Call @ref mochi::Context::DestroyAsyncScene "DestroyAsyncScene" instead.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Context::CreateScene "CreateScene", @ref mochi::Context::DestroyAsyncScene "DestroyAsyncScene"
///

/// @fn Scene* mochi::Context::GetScene(SceneHandle handle)
///
/// @brief Get a pointer to a scene by its handle.
///
/// @param[in] handle Handle to the scene.
/// @return Pointer to the scene, or nullptr if the handle is invalid in this context.
///
/// @note Call on any thread.
///

/// @fn Scene const* mochi::Context::GetScene(SceneHandle handle) const
///
/// @brief Get a const pointer to a scene by its handle.
///
/// @param[in] handle Handle to the scene.
/// @return Const pointer to the scene, or nullptr if the handle is invalid in this context.
///
/// @note Call on any thread.
///

/// @fn bool mochi::Context::IsValidScene(Scene const* scene) const
///
/// @brief Check if a scene is valid (not destroyed), and belongs to this @ref mochi::Context "Context".
///
/// @param[in] scene Pointer to the scene to check.
/// @return True if the scene is valid and belongs to this @ref mochi::Context "Context".
///
/// @note Call on any thread.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Context::CreateScene "CreateScene", @ref mochi::Context::DestroyScene "DestroyScene"
///

/// @fn AsyncScene* mochi::Context::CreateAsyncScene(std::string_view name, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Create a new @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene".
///
/// @details The returned @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene" owns a synchronous @ref mochi::Scene "Scene" and automatically steps it using a long-lived simulation task executed by the SuperDex Physics worker pool. This type of scene is often used for real-time interactive simulations where the physics rate is independent of the render rate.
///
/// @param[in] name Name of the scene to create (for debugging).
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Pointer to the new @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene", or nullptr on error. Call @ref mochi::Context::DestroyAsyncScene "DestroyAsyncScene" when done with it.
///
/// @note Must be called from a thread outside the SuperDex Physics worker pool.
/// @note Requires at least one worker thread to be available at call time. Fails if the @ref mochi::Context "Context" was initialized with zero worker threads (see @ref mochi::CreateContext "CreateContext"), if single-threaded mode is currently enabled (see @ref mochi::Context::SetIsSingleThreaded "SetIsSingleThreaded"), or if this call is made from one of the SuperDex Physics worker threads.
/// @note Do not call @ref mochi::Context::SetIsSingleThreaded "SetIsSingleThreaded" from any thread while this function is executing. Single-threaded mode must remain disabled until this function returns.
/// @note The single-threaded-mode restriction applies only during this creation call. After the @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene" is created, single-threaded mode may be enabled.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Context::DestroyAsyncScene "DestroyAsyncScene", @ref mochi::Context::IsValidAsyncScene "IsValidAsyncScene", @ref mochi::Context::CreateAsyncScenePaused "CreateAsyncScenePaused"
///

/// @fn AsyncScene* mochi::Context::CreateAsyncScenePaused(std::string_view name, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Create a new @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene" that will initially be in the paused state.
///
/// @details The returned @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene" owns a synchronous @ref mochi::Scene "Scene" and steps it using a long-lived simulation task executed by the SuperDex Physics worker pool. The scene starts paused but processes queued commands. It does not step the scene until unpaused.
///
/// @param[in] name Name of the scene to create (for debugging).
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Pointer to the new @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene", or nullptr on error. Call @ref mochi::Context::DestroyAsyncScene "DestroyAsyncScene" when done with it.
///
/// @note Must be called from a thread outside the SuperDex Physics worker pool.
/// @note Requires at least one worker thread to be available at call time. Fails if the @ref mochi::Context "Context" was initialized with zero worker threads (see @ref mochi::CreateContext "CreateContext"), if single-threaded mode is currently enabled (see @ref mochi::Context::SetIsSingleThreaded "SetIsSingleThreaded"), or if this call is made from one of the SuperDex Physics worker threads.
/// @note Do not call @ref mochi::Context::SetIsSingleThreaded "SetIsSingleThreaded" from any thread while this function is executing. Single-threaded mode must remain disabled until this function returns.
/// @note The single-threaded-mode restriction applies only during this creation call. After the @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene" is created, single-threaded mode may be enabled.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Context::CreateAsyncScene "CreateAsyncScene", @ref mochi::Context::DestroyAsyncScene "DestroyAsyncScene", @ref mochi::Context::IsValidAsyncScene "IsValidAsyncScene", @ref mochi::AsyncScene::Pause "AsyncScene::Pause", @ref mochi::AsyncScene::IsPaused "AsyncScene::IsPaused"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Context::DestroyAsyncScene(AsyncScene* scene)
///
/// @brief Immediately stop and destroy an @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene" and all its actors and constraints.
///
/// @param[in] scene Pointer to the scene to destroy
///
/// @note No-op if @p scene is null or unknown to this @ref mochi::Context "Context".
/// @note Call on any thread, except from code executed by @p scene.
/// @note Any remaining scenes will be cleaned up automatically when the @ref mochi::Context "Context" is destroyed.
///
/// @warning Do not dereference pointers to the scene, actors, constraints, etc. after this call.
/// @warning Do not call from code executed by @p scene, such as queued commands, pre/post-step callbacks, or @ref mochi::AsyncStepParams::timeStepCallback "AsyncStepParams::timeStepCallback". Destroying an @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene" is synchronous: if called from code already running on the target scene's simulation task, it can deadlock during destruction.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Context::CreateAsyncScene "CreateAsyncScene", @ref mochi::Context::IsValidAsyncScene "IsValidAsyncScene"
///

/// @fn bool mochi::Context::IsValidAsyncScene(AsyncScene const* scene) const
///
/// @brief Check if an @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene" is valid (not destroyed), and belongs to this @ref mochi::Context "Context".
///
/// @param[in] scene Pointer to the @ref mochi::AsyncScene "AsyncScene" to check
/// @return True if the scene is valid and belongs to this @ref mochi::Context "Context".
///
/// @note Call on any thread.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Context::CreateAsyncScene "CreateAsyncScene", @ref mochi::Context::DestroyAsyncScene "DestroyAsyncScene"
///

/// @fn DebugServer& mochi::Context::GetDebugServer()
///
/// @brief Get the debug server for this context.
///
/// @return Reference to the @ref mochi::DebugServer "DebugServer", which accepts connections from external debug tools.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::DebugServer "DebugServer"
///

/// @fn DebugServer const& mochi::Context::GetDebugServer() const
///
/// @brief Get a const reference to the debug server for this context.
///
/// @return Const reference to the @ref mochi::DebugServer "DebugServer".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::DebugServer "DebugServer"
///

/// @fn mochi::Context* mochi::CreateContext(int numWorkerThreads)
///
/// @brief Initialize SuperDex Physics by creating a @ref mochi::Context "Context" object.
///
/// @details You only need one Context for the entire process. It can be used to load shapes and to create any number of scenes. Call @ref mochi::DestroyContext "DestroyContext" to clean everything up when you are done.
///
/// @param[in] numWorkerThreads The number of async worker threads to initialize, or zero for single-threaded execution. Negative values (e.g. -1) let SuperDex Physics choose a default based on your CPU hardware. Positive values are clamped to the number of logical processors.
/// @return Pointer to the created @ref mochi::Context "Context".
///
/// @note Simulation performance does not necessarily improve by using more threads. For simple scenes, using a small number of threads (or even single-threaded execution) may be fastest.
/// @note Call on any thread.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::DestroyContext "DestroyContext"
///

/// @fn void mochi::DestroyContext(mochi::Context* context)
///
/// @brief Shut down SuperDex Physics by destroying the @ref mochi::Context "Context" object.
///
/// @details Any remaining state will be immediately destroyed, including all scenes, actors, and constraints.
///
/// @param[in] context The @ref mochi::Context "Context" object to destroy.
///
/// @note Passing nullptr is a no-op.
///
/// @warning Must be called on the same thread that called @ref mochi::CreateContext "CreateContext".
/// @warning Do not dereference any pointers to data owned by the @ref mochi::Context "Context" after this call.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::CreateContext "CreateContext"
///

/// @class mochi::Actor
///
/// @brief Represents a simulated body (actor) in a scene.
///
/// @note Every body in the simulation is an actor.
/// @note Actors always belong to exactly one scene.
/// @note Actors can be static or dynamic.
///
/// @warning Concurrent access to the actor or its scene is illegal.
///

/// @fn ActorHandle mochi::Actor::GetHandle() const
///
/// @brief Get the actor's handle.
///
/// @return Actor's handle.
///
/// @note Handles are safe to store and remain valid throughout the actor lifespan.
/// @note Call @ref mochi::Scene::GetActor "Scene::GetActor" to look up the actor's pointer from the actor's handle.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Scene::GetActor "Scene::GetActor"
///

/// @fn Context* mochi::Actor::GetContext()
///
/// @brief Get the @ref mochi::Context "Context" that owns this actor.
///
/// @return Pointer to the @ref mochi::Context "Context" that owns this actor.
///

/// @fn Context const* mochi::Actor::GetContext() const
///
/// @brief Get read-only access to the @ref mochi::Context "Context" that owns this actor.
///
/// @return Const pointer to the @ref mochi::Context "Context" that owns this actor.
///

/// @fn Scene* mochi::Actor::GetScene()
///
/// @brief Get the @ref mochi::Scene "Scene" that this actor belongs to.
///
/// @return Pointer to the scene that this actor belongs to.
///

/// @fn Scene const* mochi::Actor::GetScene() const
///
/// @brief Get the @ref mochi::Scene "Scene" that this actor belongs to (read only)
///
/// @return Pointer to the scene that this actor belongs to.
///

/// @fn char const* mochi::Actor::GetName() const
///
/// @brief Get the name of the actor.
///
/// @return Name of the actor.
///
/// @note Actor names are not guaranteed to be unique.
///

/// @fn ActorType mochi::Actor::GetType() const
///
/// @brief Get the type of the actor.
///
/// @return Type of the actor.
///

/// @fn ConvergenceStatus mochi::Actor::GetConvergenceStatus() const
///
/// @brief Get the convergence status of the actor in the most recent simulation step.
///
/// @return Convergence status of the actor in the most recent simulation step.
///
/// @note Static actors do not participate in the solver and may return @ref mochi::ConvergenceStatus::None "ConvergenceStatus::None".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::ConvergenceStatus "ConvergenceStatus", @ref mochi::SolverStats::convergenceStatus "SolverStats::convergenceStatus"
///

/// @fn bool mochi::Actor::IsStatic() const
///
/// @brief Check whether the actor is static.
///
/// @return True if the actor is static. False if it's dynamic.
///

/// @fn ContactParams mochi::Actor::GetContactParams(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the contact parameters of the actor.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Contact parameters of the actor.
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetContactParams(ContactParams const& params, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set the contact parameters of the actor.
///
/// @param[in] params Contact parameters to set.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///

/// @fn ColliderType mochi::Actor::GetColliderType() const
///
/// @brief Get the collider type of the actor.
///
/// @return Collider type of the actor.
///
/// @note If @ref mochi::ColliderType::Auto "ColliderType::Auto" was specified when creating the actor, this method returns the collider type that was automatically selected based on the actor's shape, not Auto.
///

/// @fn bool mochi::Actor::HasRootTransform() const
///
/// @brief Check if the actor has a root transform.
///
/// @return True if the actor has a root transform. False otherwise.
///
/// @note Non-rendered actors may not have a root transform.
///

/// @fn TransformRT mochi::Actor::GetRootTransform() const
///
/// @brief Get the actor's world-from-local transform (root transform).
///
/// @return The actor's world-from-local transform.
///
/// @note Returns an identity transform when @ref mochi::Actor::HasRootTransform "HasRootTransform" returns false.
/// @note For a top-level articulated actor, the local frame is the articulation root frame, not the root link's frame. For a nested link actor, the local frame is that link's frame.
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetRootTransform(TransformRT const& worldFromLocal, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set the actor's world-from-local transform (root transform).
///
/// @param[in] worldFromLocal World-space transform to set.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Not allowed on articulated links.
/// @note For a top-level articulated actor, the local frame is the articulation root frame, not the root link's frame.
/// @note For dynamic actors, it does not change velocity. For static actors, however, it changes velocity, because it is implicitly defined by the root transform in consecutive time steps. To cancel the velocity of a static actor, use @ref mochi::Actor::SetVelocity "SetVelocity".
/// @note Resets multi-step time integrators, e.g. BDF2 falls back to backward Euler in the first time step after this method is called.
///

/// @fn Real3 mochi::Actor::GetRigidCenterOfMassLocal(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the position of the center of mass in the actor's local coordinate frame (@ref mochi::Actor::GetRootTransform "GetRootTransform").
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Position vector of the center of mass in the actor's local coordinate frame.
///
/// @note Only supported for dynamic rigid actors (including articulated links) and soft actors.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::GetRootTransform "GetRootTransform"
///

/// @fn TransformRT mochi::Actor::GetCenterOfMassTransform(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the world-space transform of the actor expressed at the center of mass.
///
/// @details The rotation is the same as in @ref mochi::Actor::GetRootTransform "GetRootTransform", but the translation accounts for the local position of the center of mass with respect to the root transform.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Transform of the actor at the center of mass.
///
/// @note Only supported for dynamic rigid actors.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::SetCenterOfMassTransform "SetCenterOfMassTransform", @ref mochi::Actor::GetRootTransform "GetRootTransform"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetCenterOfMassTransform(TransformRT const& worldFromCom, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set the world-space transform of the actor expressed at the center of mass.
///
/// @param[in] worldFromCom World-space transform at the center of mass to set.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for dynamic rigid actors.
/// @note Does not change velocity.
/// @note Resets multi-step time integrators, e.g. BDF2 falls back to backward Euler in the first time step after this method is called.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::GetCenterOfMassTransform "GetCenterOfMassTransform", @ref mochi::Actor::SetRootTransform "SetRootTransform"
///

/// @fn Real6 mochi::Actor::GetRigidMomentOfInertiaLocal(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the moment of inertia tensor of the actor at the center of mass, aligned with the actor's local reference system (root transform), and using *negative* tensor notation.
///
/// @code
///      [ixx, ixy, ixz]   [ +∫(y²+z²)dm, -∫(xy)dm,    -∫(xz)dm     ]
///  I = [ixy, iyy, iyz] = [ -∫(xy)dm,    +∫(x²+z²)dm, -∫(yz)dm     ]
///      [ixz, iyz, izz]   [ -∫(xz)dm,    -∫(yz)dm,    +∫(x²+y²)dm  ]
/// @endcode
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Upper-right triangle in the form [ixx, ixy, ixz, iyy, iyz, izz]. Units: kg·m².
///
/// @note Only supported for dynamic rigid actors.
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetVelocity(Real3 const& linearVel, Real3 const& angularVel, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set the world-frame linear and angular velocity of the actor at the center of mass.
///
/// @param[in] linearVel Linear velocity [m/s] of the center of mass in world frame.
/// @param[in] angularVel Angular velocity [rad/s] at the center of mass in world frame.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for rigid actors (except articulated links) and soft actors (except ROMs and soft-skinned actors).
/// @note For static actors, it only supports setting zero velocity.
/// @note For soft actors, the angular velocity must be zero.
/// @note Resets multi-step time integrators, e.g. BDF2 falls back to backward Euler in the first time step after this method is called.
///

/// @fn Real3 mochi::Actor::GetLinearVelocity(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the linear velocity of the actor in world frame.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Linear velocity in world frame [m/s].
///
/// @note Only supported for rigid and soft actors.
/// @note For rigid actors, it returns the velocity of the center of mass.
/// @note For soft actors, it returns an estimate of the linear velocity of the root transform. Requires recentering to be enabled for accurate results.
/// @note Not supported for ROM actors.
///

/// @fn Real3 mochi::Actor::GetAngularVelocity(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the angular velocity of the actor in world frame.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Angular velocity in world frame [rad/s].
///
/// @note Only supported for rigid and soft actors.
/// @note For rigid actors, it returns the actual angular velocity.
/// @note For soft actors, it returns an estimate of the angular velocity of the root transform. Requires recentering to be enabled for accurate results.
/// @note Not supported for ROM actors.
///

/// @fn real mochi::Actor::GetMass(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the total mass of the actor.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Mass [kg] of the actor.
///
/// @note Not supported for static actors.
///

/// @fn real mochi::Actor::GetDensity(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the density of the actor in the undeformed configuration.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Density [kg/m³] of the actor.
///
/// @note Only supported for rigid actors (except static rigid actors), articulated links and soft actors.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::SetDensity "SetDensity", @ref mochi::Actor::GetSoftMaterialParams "GetSoftMaterialParams"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetDensity(real density, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set the density of the actor in the undeformed configuration.
///
/// @param[in] density Density [kg/m³] to set. Must be positive.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for rigid actors (except static rigid actors), articulated links and soft actors.
/// @note The moment of inertia is updated based on the new density. The center of mass is left unchanged.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::GetDensity "GetDensity", @ref mochi::Actor::SetInertiaProperties "SetInertiaProperties", @ref mochi::Actor::SetSoftMaterialParams "SetSoftMaterialParams"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetInertiaProperties(real mass, Real3 const& centerOfMass, Real6 const& momentOfInertia, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set the mass properties of the actor.
///
/// @details Directly sets mass, center of mass position in local coordinates, and moment of inertia tensor at the center of mass. This bypasses density-based computation and allows specifying exact inertia from CAD data or external measurements.
///
/// @param[in] mass Mass [kg] to set. Must be positive and finite.
/// @param[in] centerOfMass Position of center of mass [m] in actor's local coordinate frame (@ref mochi::Actor::GetRootTransform "GetRootTransform").
/// @param[in] momentOfInertia Moment of inertia tensor at center of mass [kg·m²], upper-right triangle [ixx, ixy, ixz, iyy, iyz, izz] using negative tensor notation consistent with @ref mochi::Actor::GetRigidMomentOfInertiaLocal "GetRigidMomentOfInertiaLocal". Must be finite.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for dynamic rigid actors. Not supported for static actors, soft actors, shell actors, or articulated links.
/// @note A finite but physically invalid moment of inertia tensor (negative principal moments or one violating the triangle inequality) is accepted with a warning, not rejected.
/// @note Re-anchors the density reference state. Subsequent @ref mochi::Actor::SetDensity "SetDensity" calls rescale mass and moment of inertia proportionally about the new values; center of mass is unchanged by @ref mochi::Actor::SetDensity "SetDensity".
/// @note After this call, @ref mochi::Actor::GetDensity "GetDensity" returns bulk density mass / volume.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::GetMass "GetMass", @ref mochi::Actor::GetDensity "GetDensity", @ref mochi::Actor::SetDensity "SetDensity", @ref mochi::Actor::GetRigidCenterOfMassLocal "GetRigidCenterOfMassLocal", @ref mochi::Actor::GetRigidMomentOfInertiaLocal "GetRigidMomentOfInertiaLocal"
///

/// @fn real mochi::Actor::GetElasticEnergy(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the elastic energy of the actor, measured as the difference with respect to the rest state.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Elastic energy [J] of the actor.
///
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::ElasticEnergy "QueryType::ElasticEnergy" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Requires the actor to support @ref mochi::QueryType::ElasticEnergy "QueryType::ElasticEnergy".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::QueryType::ElasticEnergy "QueryType::ElasticEnergy"
///

/// @fn RecenteringParams mochi::Actor::GetRecenteringParams() const
///
/// @brief Gets the recentering parameters of the actor.
///
/// @return Recentering parameters of the actor.
///
/// @note Recentering is only supported for soft actors (not soft-skinned). For other actor types, returns default recentering parameters with @ref mochi::RecenteringParams::useRecentering "RecenteringParams::useRecentering" set to false.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::RecenteringParams "RecenteringParams", @ref mochi::Actor::SetRecenteringParams "SetRecenteringParams"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetRecenteringParams(RecenteringParams const& params, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set the recentering parameters of the actor.
///
/// @details When enabled for a soft actor, the root transform automatically moves as the actor's "rigid pivot" (typically near the center of mass) moves.
///
/// @param[in] params Recentering parameters to set.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for soft actors (not soft-skinned).
///
/// @see @ref mochi::RecenteringParams "RecenteringParams", @ref mochi::Actor::GetRecenteringParams "GetRecenteringParams"
///

/// @fn Span<real const> mochi::Actor::GetDisplacements(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the node displacements of the actor in the actor's local frame, relative to reference (rest) positions.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Node displacements in the actor's local frame. Length is 3 × the number of nodes for soft, shell, and soft-skinned actors, or 4 × the number of nodes for rod actors (3 displacement [m] + 1 twist [rad] per node). The number of nodes is available from @ref mochi::Actor::GetMesh "GetMesh".
///
/// @note Only supported for soft, soft-skinned, shell and rod actors.
/// @note For soft-skinned actors, it returns post-skinning displacements, which may differ from the pre-skinning elastic deformation component written by @ref mochi::Actor::SetDisplacements "SetDisplacements".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::SetDisplacements "SetDisplacements", @ref mochi::Actor::GetNodePositionsLocal "GetNodePositionsLocal"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetDisplacements(Span<real const> displacements, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set the node displacements in the actor's local frame, relative to reference (rest) positions.
///
/// @param[in] displacements Node displacements [m] to set in the actor's local frame. Length must be 3 × the number of nodes. The number of nodes is available from @ref mochi::Actor::GetMesh "GetMesh".
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for soft, soft-skinned and shell actors.
/// @note For soft-skinned actors, displacements are the elastic deformation component only (before skinning is applied).
/// @note Does not change node velocities.
/// @note Resets multi-step time integrators, e.g. BDF2 falls back to backward Euler in the first time step after this method is called.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::GetDisplacements "GetDisplacements", @ref mochi::Actor::SetNodePositionsLocal "SetNodePositionsLocal"
///

/// @fn SoftMaterialParams mochi::Actor::GetSoftMaterialParams(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the material parameters of a soft actor.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Material parameters of the actor.
///
/// @note Only supported for soft actors.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::SetSoftMaterialParams "SetSoftMaterialParams", `experimental::GetSoftMaterialParamsField`, @ref mochi::Actor::GetDensity "GetDensity"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetSoftMaterialParams(SoftMaterialParams const& params, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set the material parameters of a soft actor.
///
/// @param[in] params Material parameters to set.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for soft actors.
/// @note If the @ref mochi::QueryType::ElasticEnergy "QueryType::ElasticEnergy" query is active, invalidates the elastic energy baseline. One simulation step must complete before @ref mochi::Actor::GetElasticEnergy "GetElasticEnergy" returns valid results.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::GetSoftMaterialParams "GetSoftMaterialParams", `experimental::SetSoftMaterialParamsField`, @ref mochi::Actor::SetDensity "SetDensity"
///

/// @fn MeshDataView mochi::Actor::GetMesh() const
///
/// @brief Get a view of the actor's reference simulation mesh.
///
/// @details For soft actors, returns the tetrahedral mesh. For shell actors, returns the triangle mesh. For rod actors, returns the polyline mesh. For articulated actors with a skin mesh, returns the skin mesh. For articulated actors without a skin mesh, returns an empty view. For soft-skinned actors, returns the blended skin mesh when one is present and an empty view otherwise. For rigid actors whose shape is a tetrahedral or triangular mesh, returns their surface simulation mesh. For rigid actors with an implicit shape, such as spheres and planes, returns an empty view.
///
/// @return A non-owning view of the actor's reference simulation mesh, or an empty view if the actor has no simulation mesh.
///
/// @note The returned coordinates are reference positions in the actor's local frame. They do not include deformation for deformable actors.
/// @note For rigid actors with tetrahedral or triangular mesh shapes, returns the same compact surface view as @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMesh "GetSurfaceMesh". For tetrahedral meshes this is the boundary surface. For triangular meshes, nodes not referenced by any surface triangle are omitted and remaining nodes may be reindexed. Use @ref mochi::Actor::GetReferenceShape "GetReferenceShape" and @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeMesh "Context::GetShapeMesh" to retrieve the original authored shape mesh.
/// @note The returned view remains valid until the actor is destroyed.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::MeshDataView "MeshDataView", @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMesh "GetSurfaceMesh", @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMesh "GetVisualMesh", @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeMesh "Context::GetShapeMesh"
///

/// @fn MeshDataView mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMesh() const
///
/// @brief Get a view of the actor's reference surface mesh.
///
/// @details Returns a compact triangle mesh for the actor's surface. For volumetric simulation meshes, the surface is the boundary triangles. For triangular simulation meshes, the surface has the same triangle elements as the simulation mesh, but nodes not referenced by any surface triangle are omitted and remaining nodes may be reindexed. Returns an empty view if the actor does not have a surface mesh.
///
/// @return A non-owning view of the actor's reference surface mesh, or an empty view if the actor has no surface mesh.
///
/// @note The returned coordinates are reference surface-mesh positions in the actor's local frame. They do not include deformation for deformable actors.
/// @note The returned mesh uses compact surface-node ordering. Connectivity indices refer to this ordering, which may differ from the node ordering returned by @ref mochi::Actor::GetMesh "GetMesh". Interior nodes and nodes not referenced by any surface triangle are excluded. Results from @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMeshNodePositionsLocal "GetSurfaceMeshNodePositionsLocal" and @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMeshNodeNormalsLocal "GetSurfaceMeshNodeNormalsLocal" use this same surface ordering.
/// @note The returned view remains valid until the actor is destroyed.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::MeshDataView "MeshDataView", @ref mochi::Actor::GetMesh "GetMesh", @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMesh "GetVisualMesh", @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMeshNodePositionsLocal "GetSurfaceMeshNodePositionsLocal", @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMeshNodeNormalsLocal "GetSurfaceMeshNodeNormalsLocal", @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeSurfaceMesh "Context::GetShapeSurfaceMesh"
///

/// @fn MeshDataView mochi::Actor::GetVisualMesh() const
///
/// @brief Get a view of the actor's reference visual mesh.
///
/// @details Returns a triangle mesh intended for visual rendering. The mesh may include linear visual-mesh skinning data when available. Returns an empty view if the actor does not have a visual mesh.
///
/// @return A non-owning view of the actor's reference visual mesh, or an empty view if the actor has no visual mesh.
///
/// @note The returned coordinates are reference visual-mesh positions in the actor's local frame. They do not include deformation for deformable actors.
/// @note Includes visual mesh nodes not referenced by any visual triangle. Unlike surface mesh getters, visual mesh getters do not omit unreferenced nodes.
/// @note When linear visual-mesh skinning data is present, skinning indices refer to the node ordering returned by @ref mochi::Actor::GetMesh "GetMesh", not to the compact surface-node ordering returned by @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMesh "GetSurfaceMesh". Rod visual mesh embeddings are nonlinear and are not exposed through this linear skinning field.
/// @note The returned view remains valid until the actor is destroyed.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::MeshDataView "MeshDataView", @ref mochi::Actor::GetMesh "GetMesh", @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMesh "GetSurfaceMesh", @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMeshNodePositionsLocal "GetVisualMeshNodePositionsLocal", @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMeshNodeNormalsLocal "GetVisualMeshNodeNormalsLocal", @ref mochi::Context::GetShapeVisualMesh "Context::GetShapeVisualMesh"
///

/// @fn Span<real const> mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMeshNodePositionsLocal(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the current position of the nodes (reference + displacements) of the surface mesh in the actor's local frame.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Current node positions [m] of the surface mesh in the actor's local frame (3 values per node: x, y, z). The returned node list contains exactly the nodes referenced by @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMesh "GetSurfaceMesh" and is 1-to-1 with @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMeshNodeNormalsLocal "GetSurfaceMeshNodeNormalsLocal".
///
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::SurfaceNodePositions "QueryType::SurfaceNodePositions" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Requires the actor to support @ref mochi::QueryType::SurfaceNodePositions "QueryType::SurfaceNodePositions".
/// @note The node ordering corresponds to the mesh connectivity from @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMesh "GetSurfaceMesh".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::QueryType::SurfaceNodePositions "QueryType::SurfaceNodePositions", @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMesh "GetSurfaceMesh", @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMeshNodeNormalsLocal "GetSurfaceMeshNodeNormalsLocal"
///

/// @fn Span<real const> mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMeshNodeNormalsLocal(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the normal direction for each node of the surface mesh in the actor's local frame.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Span of normals (3 values per node) in the actor's local frame, computed by normalizing the area-weighted sum of adjacent triangle normals. The returned node list contains exactly the nodes referenced by @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMesh "GetSurfaceMesh" and is 1-to-1 with @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMeshNodePositionsLocal "GetSurfaceMeshNodePositionsLocal".
///
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::SurfaceNodeNormals "QueryType::SurfaceNodeNormals" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Requires the actor to support @ref mochi::QueryType::SurfaceNodeNormals "QueryType::SurfaceNodeNormals".
/// @note The node ordering corresponds to the mesh connectivity from @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMesh "GetSurfaceMesh".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::QueryType::SurfaceNodeNormals "QueryType::SurfaceNodeNormals", @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMesh "GetSurfaceMesh", @ref mochi::Actor::GetSurfaceMeshNodePositionsLocal "GetSurfaceMeshNodePositionsLocal"
///

/// @fn ShapeHandle mochi::Actor::GetReferenceShape(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get a new @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" referencing the same shape data used to create this actor.
///
/// @details The returned handle is a new reference to the same underlying shape data. It will have a different numeric value from the @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" originally used to create the actor. The new handle represents a new request to keep the shape data in memory — the shape will remain valid as long as any handle, actor, or file cache entry references it.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return A new @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" referencing the actor's shape data.
///
/// @note In C++ and Python, the returned @ref mochi::ShapeHandle "ShapeHandle" is reference-counted and releases its reference automatically when destroyed. In the C API, you must call @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "Context::ReleaseShape" when done with the handle to avoid leaks.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Context::ReleaseShape "Context::ReleaseShape", @ref mochi::Context::LoadShapeFromFile "Context::LoadShapeFromFile"
///

/// @fn std::string_view mochi::Actor::GetContactLayer() const
///
/// @brief Get the name of the contact layer of the actor.
///
/// @return Contact layer name, or an empty string if the actor has no contact layer.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::SetContactLayer "SetContactLayer", @ref mochi::Scene::EnableLayerContactAsymmetric "Scene::EnableLayerContactAsymmetric", @ref mochi::Scene::EnableLayerContactSymmetric "Scene::EnableLayerContactSymmetric"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetContactLayer(std::string_view const& layer)
///
/// @brief Set the name of the contact layer of the actor.
///
/// @param[in] layer Contact layer name to set.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::GetContactLayer "GetContactLayer", @ref mochi::Scene::EnableLayerContactAsymmetric "Scene::EnableLayerContactAsymmetric", @ref mochi::Scene::EnableLayerContactSymmetric "Scene::EnableLayerContactSymmetric"
///

/// @fn int mochi::Actor::GetNumDofs() const
///
/// @brief Get the number of degrees of freedom (DoFs) of the actor.
///
/// @return Number of degrees of freedom of the actor.
///
/// @note Returns zero for actors without degrees of freedom (e.g., static actors).
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::GetDofValues(Span<int const> dofIndices, Span<real> outDofValues, Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the current value of the actor's degrees of freedom (DoFs) corresponding to the specified indices.
///
/// @param[in] dofIndices DoF indices to query. Each index must be in the range [0, @ref mochi::Actor::GetNumDofs "GetNumDofs"). If empty, get the value of all DoFs.
/// @param[out] outDofValues Output buffer for the DoF values. Size must equal @ref mochi::Actor::GetNumDofs "GetNumDofs" when @p dofIndices is empty, or the size of @p dofIndices otherwise.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Not supported for static actors, even when both input and output spans are empty.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::GetNumDofs "GetNumDofs"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::QueryNodesInVolumeLocal(Aabb const& volume, bool boundaryOnly, std::function<void(int, Real3)> const& callback, Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Find the actor's nodes that are inside an axis-aligned bounding box (AABB).
///
/// @param[in] volume Axis-aligned bounding box in the actor's local frame.
/// @param[in] boundaryOnly If true, only boundary nodes are considered.
/// @param[in] callback Callback called for each node found. The position is the current node position [m] in the actor's local frame. The node index uses @ref mochi::Actor::GetMesh "GetMesh" ordering, including when @p boundaryOnly is true.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note When @p boundaryOnly is false, this function supports only soft and shell actors. When true, it also supports articulated actors with a skin mesh, soft-skinned actors with a blended skin mesh, and rigid actors (dynamic or static) with tetrahedral or triangular mesh shapes. Rod actors and actors without a simulation mesh are not supported.
/// @note Requires query registration before the simulation step. Register @ref mochi::QueryType::NodePositions "QueryType::NodePositions" when @p boundaryOnly is false, or @ref mochi::QueryType::SurfaceNodePositions "QueryType::SurfaceNodePositions" when @p boundaryOnly is true. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
///
/// @warning This is a synchronous call and may be expensive.
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::QueryNodesInVolumeLocal(Obb const& volume, bool boundaryOnly, std::function<void(int, Real3)> const& callback, Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Find the actor's nodes that are inside an oriented bounding box (OBB).
///
/// @param[in] volume Oriented bounding box in the actor's local frame.
/// @param[in] boundaryOnly If true, only boundary nodes are considered.
/// @param[in] callback Callback called for each node found. The position is the current node position [m] in the actor's local frame. The node index uses @ref mochi::Actor::GetMesh "GetMesh" ordering, including when @p boundaryOnly is true.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note When @p boundaryOnly is false, this function supports only soft and shell actors. When true, it also supports articulated actors with a skin mesh, soft-skinned actors with a blended skin mesh, and rigid actors (dynamic or static) with tetrahedral or triangular mesh shapes. Rod actors and actors without a simulation mesh are not supported.
/// @note Requires query registration before the simulation step. Register @ref mochi::QueryType::NodePositions "QueryType::NodePositions" when @p boundaryOnly is false, or @ref mochi::QueryType::SurfaceNodePositions "QueryType::SurfaceNodePositions" when @p boundaryOnly is true. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
///
/// @warning This is a synchronous call and may be expensive.
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::QueryNodesInVolumeLocal(Sphere const& volume, bool boundaryOnly, std::function<void(int, Real3)> const& callback, Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Find the actor's nodes that are inside a sphere.
///
/// @param[in] volume Sphere in the actor's local frame.
/// @param[in] boundaryOnly If true, only boundary nodes are considered.
/// @param[in] callback Callback called for each node found. The position is the current node position [m] in the actor's local frame. The node index uses @ref mochi::Actor::GetMesh "GetMesh" ordering, including when @p boundaryOnly is true.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note When @p boundaryOnly is false, this function supports only soft and shell actors. When true, it also supports articulated actors with a skin mesh, soft-skinned actors with a blended skin mesh, and rigid actors (dynamic or static) with tetrahedral or triangular mesh shapes. Rod actors and actors without a simulation mesh are not supported.
/// @note Requires query registration before the simulation step. Register @ref mochi::QueryType::NodePositions "QueryType::NodePositions" when @p boundaryOnly is false, or @ref mochi::QueryType::SurfaceNodePositions "QueryType::SurfaceNodePositions" when @p boundaryOnly is true. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
///
/// @warning This is a synchronous call and may be expensive.
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::GetPointsDistanceToSurface(Span<Real3 const> pointsWorld, Span<real> outDistances, Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Query the signed distance to the closest point on the actor's surface.
///
/// @param[in] pointsWorld Point cloud in world frame.
/// @param[out] outDistances Output distances [m], in the same order as the input points. Must be the same size as the input points. Negative values indicate points inside the actor.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Requires the actor to have a collider.
/// @note For actors with SDF collider, the reported distance is only correct inside the actor's bounding box. Outside the bounding box, it is an upper bound based on the triangle inequality.
/// @note This function is not supported for soft actors or for the experimental @ref mochi::ColliderType::PointCloud "ColliderType::PointCloud".
///

/// @fn Aabb mochi::Actor::GetAabbLocal(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get an axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) that contains the full volume of the actor, in the actor's local frame.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return AABB in the actor's local frame containing the full actor volume.
///

/// @fn Aabb mochi::Actor::GetAabbWorld(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get an axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) that contains the full volume of the actor, in world frame.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return AABB in world frame containing the full actor volume.
///

/// @fn Span<real const> mochi::Actor::GetNodePositionsLocal(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the current position (reference + displacements) of each node in the actor's local frame.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Flattened node positions [m] in the actor's local frame (3 values per node: x, y, z).
///
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::NodePositions "QueryType::NodePositions" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Requires the actor to support @ref mochi::QueryType::NodePositions "QueryType::NodePositions".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::QueryType::NodePositions "QueryType::NodePositions"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetZeroDisplacementsAndVelocities(Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set all local displacement and velocity DoFs to zero.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for soft, soft-skinned, shell and rod actors.
/// @note For soft-skinned actors, it zeroes the elastic deformation and velocity only. The skeleton-driven pose is unaffected.
/// @note For rod actors, it zeroes both the translational displacement DoFs and the twist-angle DoFs.
/// @note Resets multi-step time integrators, e.g. BDF2 falls back to backward Euler in the first time step after this method is called.
///

/// @fn Span<real const> mochi::Actor::GetElementsDeformationGradient(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the deformation gradient of each element.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Span of deformation gradients. The deformation gradient F of element e is stored at index e*9 in row-major format: F_00, F_01, F_02, F_10, F_11, F_12, F_20, F_21, F_22.
///
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::ElementsDeformationGradient "QueryType::ElementsDeformationGradient" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Requires the actor to support @ref mochi::QueryType::ElementsDeformationGradient "QueryType::ElementsDeformationGradient".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::QueryType::ElementsDeformationGradient "QueryType::ElementsDeformationGradient"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetNodePositionsLocal(Span<real const> positionsLocal, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set the current position of each node (reference + displacements) in the actor's local frame.
///
/// @param[in] positionsLocal Node positions [m] to set (3 values per node: x, y, z) in the actor's local frame.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for soft (not soft-skinned) and shell actors.
/// @note Does not change node velocities.
/// @note Resets multi-step time integrators, e.g. BDF2 falls back to backward Euler in the first time step after this method is called.
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetNodeVelocitiesLocal(Span<real const> velocitiesLocal, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set the current velocity of each node in the actor's local frame.
///
/// @param[in] velocitiesLocal Node velocities to set in the actor's local frame.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for soft (not soft-skinned), shell and rod actors.
/// @note For soft and shell actors: 3 values per node [m/s] — (vx, vy, vz).
/// @note For rod actors: 4 values per node — (vx, vy, vz) in [m/s] plus a twist rate [rad/s].
/// @note Resets multi-step time integrators, e.g. BDF2 falls back to backward Euler in the first time step after this method is called.
///

/// @fn Span<real const> mochi::Actor::GetVisualMeshNodePositionsLocal(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the current position (reference + displacements) of the nodes of the visual mesh in the actor's local frame.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Current node positions [m] of the visual mesh in the actor's local frame (3 values per node: x, y, z). The number of nodes is available via @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMesh "GetVisualMesh". The order of the nodes is 1-to-1 with @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMeshNodeNormalsLocal "GetVisualMeshNodeNormalsLocal".
///
/// @note Includes visual mesh nodes not referenced by any visual triangle. Unlike surface mesh getters, visual mesh getters do not omit unreferenced nodes.
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::VisualNodePositions "QueryType::VisualNodePositions" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Requires the actor to support @ref mochi::QueryType::VisualNodePositions "QueryType::VisualNodePositions".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::QueryType::VisualNodePositions "QueryType::VisualNodePositions", @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMesh "GetVisualMesh", @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMeshNodeNormalsLocal "GetVisualMeshNodeNormalsLocal"
///

/// @fn Span<real const> mochi::Actor::GetVisualMeshNodeNormalsLocal(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the normal direction to each node of the visual mesh in the actor's local frame.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Flattened normals (3 values per node: nx, ny, nz) in the actor's local frame. The number of nodes is available via @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMesh "GetVisualMesh". The order of the nodes is 1-to-1 with @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMeshNodePositionsLocal "GetVisualMeshNodePositionsLocal". Normals for visual nodes not referenced by any visual triangle are zero.
///
/// @note Includes visual mesh nodes not referenced by any visual triangle. Unlike surface mesh getters, visual mesh getters do not omit unreferenced nodes.
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::VisualNodeNormals "QueryType::VisualNodeNormals" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Requires the actor to support @ref mochi::QueryType::VisualNodeNormals "QueryType::VisualNodeNormals".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::QueryType::VisualNodeNormals "QueryType::VisualNodeNormals", @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMesh "GetVisualMesh", @ref mochi::Actor::GetVisualMeshNodePositionsLocal "GetVisualMeshNodePositionsLocal"
///

/// @fn Span<int const> mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices() const
///
/// @brief Get the DoF indices that are constrained by boundary conditions.
///
/// @return Span of DoF indices with boundary conditions applied.
///
/// @note See @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld" for the DoF layout for each actor type.
/// @note The returned span contains every boundary-condition entry added through the public boundary-condition functions that has not been cleared, in the order the entries were added, including repeated DoF indices. Permanent and clearable entries are both included and are not distinguishable. Boundary conditions applied automatically by the engine are not included.
/// @note Adding boundary conditions or calling @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions" may invalidate the returned span. Do not retain it across either operation. Permanent entries are retained when @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions" is called, but their positions within subsequently returned spans may change. Do not cache those positions across a call to @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofValuesWorld "GetBoundaryConditionDofValuesWorld", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld"
///

/// @fn Span<real const> mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofValuesWorld() const
///
/// @brief Get the target values of DoFs fixed by boundary conditions.
///
/// @return Span of DoF target values in the actor-specific representations documented by @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld".
///
/// @note 1-to-1 correspondence with @ref mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices "GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices".
/// @note Adding boundary conditions or calling @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions" may invalidate the returned span. Do not retain it across either operation. Permanent entries are retained when @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions" is called, but their positions within subsequently returned spans may change. Do not cache those positions across a call to @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices "GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld(Span<int const> dofIndices, Span<real const> dofValuesWorld, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Add boundary conditions to specified DoFs.
///
/// @param[in] dofIndices DoF indices to constrain.
/// @param[in] dofValuesWorld Target values in the actor-specific representations described below. Length must equal @p dofIndices.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Not supported for nested soft actors (see @ref mochi::Actor::GetNestedSoftActors "GetNestedSoftActors").
/// @note Not supported in differentiable scenes (`diffsim::MakeSceneDifferentiable`) or for ROM actors.
/// @note For soft and shell actors, each node has 3 consecutive DoFs containing its target x, y, and z position [m] in the world frame. All 3 must be specified together. Consider @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorld "AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorld" as a more convenient alternative.
/// @note For rigid and articulated actors, the DoF indices within each call must be sorted in strictly increasing order (no duplicate indices).
/// @note Rigid actors have 6 DoFs: indices 0-2 are the target world-space center-of-mass position [m], and indices 3-5 are the target world-from-local orientation as a rotation vector (axis multiplied by angle [rad]). Either all or none of the 3 rotation DoFs must be specified.
/// @note Articulated actors have a number of DoFs that depends on the number of joints and the DoFs per joint. When setting boundary conditions on the rotation of a free or spherical joint, either all or none of the 3 DoFs must be specified.
/// @note Rod actors have 4 DoFs per node: the first 3 values are the target node x, y, and z position [m] in the world frame, followed by the next element's scalar twist angle [rad]. (For open rods, the last DoF, i.e., the final node's twist DoF, is included for padding only, does not affect the physics, and is automatically constrained to zero. This automatic constraint is not reported by @ref mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices "GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices". For closed-loop rods, all twist DoFs are physical.) Boundary conditions on a rod node's position must specify all 3 consecutive displacement DoFs for that node. Only zero values are allowed for the scalar twist angle in this function, with the interpretation that the element's cross-section material axes rotate by only the minimal amount needed to remain orthogonal to the rod's centerline. More elaborate control over rod element rotations should use constraints instead of boundary conditions.
/// @note Boundary condition APIs add to existing boundary conditions; they do not replace existing entries. If a DoF has more than one entry, getter APIs return all entries in the order they were added, and the most recently added value is the effective value during the step.
/// @note Boundary conditions can be cleared with @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions".
///
/// @warning Constrained 3D rotations may exhibit small numerical differences due to differences in the internal representation.
/// @warning Adding a boundary condition to the same DoF more than once is legal — the most recently added value wins — but strongly discouraged. Each call adds an entry, so repeatedly re-adding without an intervening @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions" grows the per-step cost without bound. To update a boundary condition, call @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions" and add it again.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorld "AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorld", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent", @ref mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices "GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices", @ref mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofValuesWorld "GetBoundaryConditionDofValuesWorld"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent(Span<int const> dofIndices, Span<real const> dofValuesWorld, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Add permanent boundary conditions to specified DoFs.
///
/// @param[in] dofIndices DoF indices to constrain.
/// @param[in] dofValuesWorld Target values in the actor-specific representations documented by @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld". Length must equal @p dofIndices.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Not supported for nested soft actors (see @ref mochi::Actor::GetNestedSoftActors "GetNestedSoftActors").
/// @note Not supported in differentiable scenes (`diffsim::MakeSceneDifferentiable`) or for ROM actors.
/// @note Same as @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld", except boundary conditions cannot be cleared.
/// @note If a clearable entry is later added for the same DoF, that clearable entry is the effective value until @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions" removes it. The permanent entry is then the effective value again.
///
/// @warning Permanent boundary conditions are retained for the lifetime of the actor and cannot be removed by @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions". Adding a permanent boundary condition to the same DoF more than once is legal but strongly discouraged. The duplicates can never be cleared and irreversibly grow the per-step cost. Add each permanent boundary condition only once.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorld(Span<int const> nodeIndices, Span<real const> nodePositionsWorld, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Add world-space boundary conditions for specified nodes.
///
/// @param[in] nodeIndices Node indices to constrain.
/// @param[in] nodePositionsWorld Target positions [m] in world frame. Length must be 3 times the size of @p nodeIndices.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for soft and shell actors, except nested soft actors (see @ref mochi::Actor::GetNestedSoftActors "GetNestedSoftActors").
/// @note Not supported in differentiable scenes (`diffsim::MakeSceneDifferentiable`) or for ROM actors.
/// @note Boundary conditions can be cleared with @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions".
/// @note Equivalent to calling @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld" with DoF indices (3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2) for each node i.
/// @note This API adds to existing boundary conditions. See @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld" for behavior when a DoF has more than one entry.
///
/// @warning Adding boundary conditions to the same nodes repeatedly without clearing grows the per-step cost without bound. See @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorldPermanent "AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorldPermanent", @ref mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices "GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices", @ref mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofValuesWorld "GetBoundaryConditionDofValuesWorld"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorldPermanent(Span<int const> nodeIndices, Span<real const> nodePositionsWorld, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Add permanent world-space boundary conditions for specified nodes.
///
/// @param[in] nodeIndices Node indices to constrain.
/// @param[in] nodePositionsWorld Target positions [m] in world frame. Length must be 3 times the size of @p nodeIndices.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for soft and shell actors, except nested soft actors (see @ref mochi::Actor::GetNestedSoftActors "GetNestedSoftActors").
/// @note Not supported in differentiable scenes (`diffsim::MakeSceneDifferentiable`) or for ROM actors.
/// @note Same as @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorld "AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorld", except boundary conditions cannot be cleared.
/// @note See @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent" for interaction with clearable entries later added to the same DoF.
///
/// @warning Add each permanent boundary condition only once. Duplicates can never be cleared and irreversibly grow the per-step cost. See @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorld "AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorld", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionConstrainedNodesAtRest(Error& error)
///
/// @brief Fix the "constrained nodes" at their world-space reference positions.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for soft and shell actors, except nested soft actors (see @ref mochi::Actor::GetNestedSoftActors "GetNestedSoftActors").
/// @note Not supported in differentiable scenes (`diffsim::MakeSceneDifferentiable`) or for ROM actors.
/// @note Boundary conditions can be cleared with @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions".
/// @note Applies to constrained nodes specified by the actor's mesh. Has no effect if none are specified.
/// @note Each target position is computed by transforming the node's mesh reference coordinate by the actor's root transform.
/// @note This API adds to existing boundary conditions. See @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld" for behavior when a DoF has more than one entry.
///
/// @warning If the actor's mesh has constrained nodes, calling this repeatedly without clearing re-adds the same boundary conditions and grows the per-step cost without bound. See @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions "ClearBoundaryConditions", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionConstrainedNodesAtRestPermanent "AddBoundaryConditionConstrainedNodesAtRestPermanent", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionConstrainedNodesAtRestPermanent(Error& error)
///
/// @brief Permanently fix the "constrained nodes" at their world-space reference positions.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for soft and shell actors, except nested soft actors (see @ref mochi::Actor::GetNestedSoftActors "GetNestedSoftActors").
/// @note Not supported in differentiable scenes (`diffsim::MakeSceneDifferentiable`) or for ROM actors.
/// @note Same as @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionConstrainedNodesAtRest "AddBoundaryConditionConstrainedNodesAtRest", except boundary conditions cannot be cleared.
/// @note See @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent" for interaction with clearable entries later added to the same DoF.
///
/// @warning If the actor's mesh has constrained nodes, each call adds a permanent boundary condition for every constrained node. Call this at most once. Repeated calls create duplicates that cannot be removed and irreversibly grow the per-step cost. See @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionConstrainedNodesAtRest "AddBoundaryConditionConstrainedNodesAtRest", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorldPermanent"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::ClearBoundaryConditions()
///
/// @brief Remove all clearable boundary conditions previously added.
///
/// @note To replace existing clearable boundary conditions, call this before adding the new boundary-condition set.
/// @note May invalidate spans previously returned by @ref mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices "GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices" and @ref mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofValuesWorld "GetBoundaryConditionDofValuesWorld". Do not retain them across this call.
/// @note Permanent entries are retained, but this call may change their positions in spans returned by @ref mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices "GetBoundaryConditionDofIndices" and @ref mochi::Actor::GetBoundaryConditionDofValuesWorld "GetBoundaryConditionDofValuesWorld". Do not cache those positions across this call.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorld "AddBoundaryConditionNodesWorld", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionConstrainedNodesAtRest "AddBoundaryConditionConstrainedNodesAtRest"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetExternalForcesOnDofs(Span<int const> dofIndices, Span<real const> forceValues, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set external forces on specified DoFs.
///
/// @param[in] dofIndices DoF indices to apply forces to. Must be unique.
/// @param[in] forceValues Force values [N] for translation DoFs, torque values [N·m] for rotation DoFs. Length must equal the number of DoF indices.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Only supported for rigid, articulated, rod, and shell actors.
/// @note DoF indices use the same per-actor-type index layout documented by @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld".
/// @note External forces can be cleared with @ref mochi::Actor::ClearExternalForces "ClearExternalForces".
/// @note Replaces all previously set external forces, including external forces on DoFs not included in @p dofIndices. Passing empty @p dofIndices and @p forceValues is equivalent to calling @ref mochi::Actor::ClearExternalForces "ClearExternalForces".
/// @note For rigid and shell actors, values are interpreted in the world frame.
/// @note For articulated actors, values are generalized forces in the actor's joint-DoF coordinate basis.
/// @note For rod actors, forces on displacement DoFs are specified in the world frame, while (generalized) forces (scalar torques) on element twist-angle DoFs are always oriented along the corresponding element's current orientation.
/// @note For open (non-closed-loop) rod actors, the last DoF is padding that does not participate in physics, so it is invalid to apply a torque to it. For closed-loop rods, the last DoF is a physical twist angle.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::ClearExternalForces "ClearExternalForces", @ref mochi::Actor::GetExternalForces "GetExternalForces", @ref mochi::Actor::AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld "AddBoundaryConditionDofsWorld"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::ClearExternalForces()
///
/// @brief Remove all the external forces previously added.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::SetExternalForcesOnDofs "SetExternalForcesOnDofs"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::GetExternalForces(Span<real> outForces, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Get the external forces currently set on this actor as a dense array over all DoFs.
///
/// @param[out] outForces Dense output array of force values [N] for translation DoFs and torque values [N·m] for rotation DoFs. One entry per DoF. Size must equal @ref mochi::Actor::GetNumDofs "GetNumDofs". DoFs with no external force set are filled with zero.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
/// @note Returned values use the same frame convention as @ref mochi::Actor::SetExternalForcesOnDofs "SetExternalForcesOnDofs".
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::SetExternalForcesOnDofs "SetExternalForcesOnDofs", @ref mochi::Actor::ClearExternalForces "ClearExternalForces"
///

/// @fn Span<ContactPoint const> mochi::Actor::GetContactPointsWorld(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get all the active contact points of the actor.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Span of active contact points.
///
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::ContactPoints "QueryType::ContactPoints" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Requires the actor to support @ref mochi::QueryType::ContactPoints "QueryType::ContactPoints".
/// @note If the solver diverged in the last simulation step, results may not be available or may be stale.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::ContactPoint "ContactPoint", @ref mochi::QueryType::ContactPoints "QueryType::ContactPoints"
///

/// @fn Span<NodeContactForce const> mochi::Actor::GetNodeContactForcesWorld(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get contact forces on nodes.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Span of per-node contact forces [N] in world frame.
///
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::NodeContactForces "QueryType::NodeContactForces" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Requires the actor to support @ref mochi::QueryType::NodeContactForces "QueryType::NodeContactForces".
/// @note If the solver diverged in the last simulation step, results may not be available or may be stale.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::NodeContactForce "NodeContactForce", @ref mochi::QueryType::NodeContactForces "QueryType::NodeContactForces"
///

/// @fn Real3 mochi::Actor::GetContactForceWorld(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the total contact force on the actor.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Total contact force [N] in world frame.
///
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::TotalContactForce "QueryType::TotalContactForce" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Requires the actor to support @ref mochi::QueryType::TotalContactForce "QueryType::TotalContactForce".
/// @note If the solver diverged in the last simulation step, results may not be available or may be stale.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::Actor::GetContactTorqueWorld "GetContactTorqueWorld", @ref mochi::Actor::GetContactForceFromActorWorld "GetContactForceFromActorWorld", @ref mochi::QueryType::TotalContactForce "QueryType::TotalContactForce"
///

/// @fn Real3 mochi::Actor::GetContactTorqueWorld(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the total contact torque about the center of mass.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Total contact torque [N·m] in world frame, about the center of mass.
///
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::TotalContactForce "QueryType::TotalContactForce" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Only supported for rigid actors and articulated links that support @ref mochi::QueryType::TotalContactForce "QueryType::TotalContactForce".
/// @note If the solver diverged in the last simulation step, results may not be available or may be stale.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::Actor::GetContactForceWorld "GetContactForceWorld", @ref mochi::QueryType::TotalContactForce "QueryType::TotalContactForce"
///

/// @fn Real3 mochi::Actor::GetContactForceFromActorWorld(Actor const* other, Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get the total contact force on the actor from another specified actor.
///
/// @param[in] other Actor exerting the contact force on this actor.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return Total contact force [N] in world frame from the specified actor.
///
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::TotalContactForce "QueryType::TotalContactForce" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Requires the actor to support @ref mochi::QueryType::TotalContactForce "QueryType::TotalContactForce".
/// @note If the solver diverged in the last simulation step, results may not be available or may be stale.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::Actor::GetContactForceWorld "GetContactForceWorld", @ref mochi::QueryType::TotalContactForce "QueryType::TotalContactForce"
///

/// @fn SdfDistances mochi::Actor::GetSdfDistances(Error& error) const
///
/// @brief Get SDF distances for contact sample points.
///
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return SDF distance information for contact sample points.
///
/// @note Requires registering @ref mochi::QueryType::SdfDistances "QueryType::SdfDistances" before the simulation step. Results are available after the simulation step completes.
/// @note Requires the actor to support @ref mochi::QueryType::SdfDistances "QueryType::SdfDistances".
/// @note If the solver diverged in the last simulation step, results may not be available or may be stale.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::SdfDistances "SdfDistances", @ref mochi::QueryType::SdfDistances "QueryType::SdfDistances"
///

/// @fn QueryHandle mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery(QueryType type, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Register a query to compute data for this actor.
///
/// @param[in] type Type of query to register.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return @ref mochi::QueryHandle "QueryHandle" for the registered query, or an invalid handle if registration fails.
///
/// @note Queries may add substantial computational overhead. Use only when necessary.
/// @note Data is available after the next simulation step, even if its time step is zero.
/// @note Call @ref mochi::Actor::CancelQuery "CancelQuery" when the query is not needed again in the future.
/// @note Queries are reference counted internally, so they will be available as long as there is one outstanding @ref mochi::QueryHandle "QueryHandle".
/// @note Registration is all-or-nothing: if registration fails, no query is registered.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::CancelQuery "CancelQuery", @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQueryAndCompute "RegisterQueryAndCompute", @ref mochi::Actor::IsQuerySupported "IsQuerySupported", @ref mochi::Constraint::RegisterQuery "Constraint::RegisterQuery"
///

/// @fn QueryHandle mochi::Actor::RegisterQueryAndCompute(QueryType type, Error& error)
///
/// @brief Register a query for this actor and compute the result immediately.
///
/// @param[in] type Type of query to register.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
/// @return @ref mochi::QueryHandle "QueryHandle" for the registered query.
///
/// @note Same as @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", except that the data is computed immediately (blocking) rather than at the next simulation step.
/// @note Immediate computation is not supported for all query types. For unsupported types, the query is still registered successfully, immediate computation is skipped, and data becomes available after the next simulation step. See @ref mochi::QueryType "QueryType" documentation for which types support immediate computation.
/// @note Stepping the scene with zero time step is another way to force queries to update, without advancing the state of the simulation.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::Actor::CancelQuery "CancelQuery"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::CancelQuery(QueryHandle handle)
///
/// @brief Cancel a previously registered query.
///
/// @param[in] handle @ref mochi::QueryHandle "QueryHandle" from @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery" or @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQueryAndCompute "RegisterQueryAndCompute".
///
/// @note Cancelling an invalid or already-cancelled handle has no effect.
/// @note Cancelling queries may improve memory usage and/or performance if the query is no longer needed.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery", @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQueryAndCompute "RegisterQueryAndCompute"
///

/// @fn bool mochi::Actor::IsQuerySupported(QueryType type) const
///
/// @brief Check whether a query type is supported for this actor.
///
/// @param[in] type Type of query to check.
/// @return True if @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery" would succeed for this query type, false otherwise.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::RegisterQuery "RegisterQuery"
///

/// @fn void mochi::Actor::SetUserData(void* userData)
///
/// @brief Set application-specific user data for this actor.
///
/// @param[in] userData Pointer to user data, or nullptr to clear.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::GetUserData "GetUserData"
///

/// @fn void* mochi::Actor::GetUserData() const
///
/// @brief Get application-specific user data for this actor.
///
/// @return Pointer to user data, or nullptr if none has been set.
///
/// @see @ref mochi::Actor::SetUserData "SetUserData"
///

